  "english": "26. Sunday [Tone 6, Third Side, BZ]. Fifth. Canticle [Harts] Tone 6 [gk]: \"Pre-eternal\" (Nakhayavedyan). Evening Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 3 [b3]: \"Today they rejoiced\" (Aysor zvartchatsan).\n\n29. Wednesday, Tone 6 [GK]. Canticle [Harts] Tone 8 [dk]: \"Blessed are You Lord God, blessed.\" Prep-day [Barekendan] of the Nativity Fast.\n\nJanuary:\n\n2. Sunday, Tone 2 [AK]. Sixth Sunday of the Fast. Evening Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 6 [gk]: \"Wondrous Resurrection\" (Hrashali zyarutyun).\n\n5. Wednesday, Tone 5 [GDZ]. Candlemas [Eve / Chragaloyts] of the Nativity of Christ.\n\n19. Sunday, Tone 4 [BK]. Fourth [Sunday]. Canticle [Harts] Tone 5 [g3]: \"Glorified\" (Paravorial). Evening Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 4 [bk]: \"Christ is risen\" (Kristos yaryav), and Morning [Hymn] \"They anticipated\" (Kankhetsin).\n\n20. Monday, Tone 5 [GZ]. Ignatius and Addeus, patriarchs, and Maruthas, and Theopompus, bishops, and Theonas the martyr, and the four soldiers, etc.\n\n21. Tuesday, Tone 6 [GK]. King Abgar. Read the Lections and Gospel for [King] Theodosius.\n\n23. Thursday, Tone 8 [DK]. David the prophet and James the apostle.\n\nTHE SEVEN-WEEK CYCLE OF THE ROMANS 4.\n\nFebruary:\n\n14. Saturday. Presentation of the Lord [Tyarnndaraj].\n\n15. Sunday, Tone 8 [DK]. Sunday of Great Lent [Bun Barekendan]. See the order in the First Volume until Vardavar, keeping the order of the Holy [Churches].\n\nApril:\n\n5. Sunday, Tone 1 [AZ]. Easter [Zatik]. Day of the Resurrection of Christ.\n\n7. Tuesday, Tone 3 [BZ]. Feast of the Annunciation of the Holy Virgin.\n\nMay:\n\n14. Thursday, Tone 8 [DK]. Ascension of Christ.\n\n24. Sunday, Tone 2 [AK]. Pentecost [Coming of the Holy Spirit]. Prep-day [Barekendan] of the Fast of Elijah.\n\n31. Sunday, Tone 1 [ACH]. First. Beginning of the Sundays of the Resurrection. Canticle [Harts] Tone 1 [ad]: \"Who came for the salvation of the universe\" (Vor yekir i prkutyun tiezerats).\n\nJanuary:\n\n6. TUESDAY. Feast of the Nativity and Epiphany of Christ. The meat-eating period [mitsoch utikn] is twenty days.\n\n15. Thursday. John the Forerunner [Karapet].\n\n17. Saturday. Peter the patriarch, Blaise, etc.\n\n18. Sunday. First [Sunday]. Canticle [Harts] Tone 5 [gdz]: \"Dawn of the Only-Begotten\" (Tsagumn miatsni).\n\n19. Monday. Antony, and Tryphon, Barsama, and Onuphrius, the hermits.\n\n20. Tuesday. King Theodosius, and the Holy Infants of Ephesus.\n\n22. Thursday. Cyriacus and Julitta, and Vahan of Goghtn, and Gordius, Polyeuctus, and Grigoris.\n\n24. Saturday. The one hundred and fifty holy patriarchs of the Council of Constantinople.\n\n25. Sunday. Second [Sunday]. Prep-day [Barekendan] of the Fast of Catechumens [Arachavorats]. See the order in the First Volume.",
